@@ -43,3 +43,39 @@ composition, and an actual GPU caster→receiver check using an opaque/transpare
 texture. The GPU test explicitly reports a skip without an adapter; setting
 `AURORA_REQUIRE_GPU=1` makes that condition fail, as the Aurora preview launcher does.
 Final visual quality and performance must be checked in the running game.
+
+## shadow.2: fixed quality recipes
+
+`0.1-aurora-shadow.2` additionally requires a material stage and this manifest table:
+
+```toml
+[sun_shadows]
+quality = "high" # low, medium, high, ultra; exact lowercase names
+```
+
+Other API lines reject the table. Old shadow.1 still uses its original 2048² map,
+receiver code and ABI. shadow.2 keeps the same 80-byte uniform and water.3 frame ABI.
+The checked manifest carries its recipe through compilation to GPU allocation.
+
+| Quality | Depth32Float map | Raw depth storage | Projection half-width | Receiver fade | PCF taps |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Low | 1² dummy | 4 bytes, excluding driver overhead | unused | disabled | none executed |
+| Medium | 1024² | 4 MiB | 36 blocks | 22–32 blocks | 9 |
+| High | 2048² | 16 MiB | 48 blocks | 32–44 blocks | 9 |
+| Ultra | 4096² | 64 MiB | 68 blocks | 48–64 blocks | 25 |
+
+Low returns no light view and skips the entire native shadow render pass (including
+its clear); its receiver uniform disables sampling. A dummy texture and the pipeline
+remain bound. It is not merely `shadow_strength=0`. Other effects are unaffected.
+Ultra's caster radius is 128 blocks instead of 96; actual coverage also depends on
+loaded terrain/detail distance. All levels retain the 0.1–256 light-space depth span.
+Receiver bias scales with world texel width relative to High. Filter constants are
+engine-owned WGSL generated from the recipe, not pack overrides that could disagree
+with allocated resources. High's receiver is mathematically the shadow.1 receiver.
+
+Tests cover all recipes in Metal/SPIR-V/HLSL translation and real terrain composition,
+strict manifest version gating, and camera translation at positive/negative coordinates
+up to the world border at multiple solar angles. `quality_levels_on_gpu` tests Low's
+unrendered dummy fallback plus opaque/cutout reception on the other three map sizes;
+the legacy GPU test remains separate. Live preset switching, moving sun/camera,
+contact bias, water transitions and comparative GPU cost still need game validation.
